<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75297" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρομαι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>keep watch,</i> used only in compd. with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί,</span> which is always separated from the
			Verb by tmesis, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰπόλια πλατἔ αἰγῶν . . ἐσχατιῇ
					βόσκοντ᾽, ἐπὶ δ᾽ ἀνέρες ἐσθλοὶ ὄρονται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					14.104
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ δ᾽ ἀνέρες ἐσθλοὶ ὄροντο, οἶνον
					οἰνοχοεῦντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					3.471
				</span></i>
			 (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρνυμι</span> ad init.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ δ᾽ ἀνὴρ ἐσθλὸς ὀρώρει Μηριόνης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					23.112
				</span></i>
			.—So Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				14.104
			</span></i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅρει: φυλάσσει,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>) rightly : <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ . .
			ὄρομαι</span> is related to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίουρος
				ʽἔφοροσ̓.</span></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
